WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B one.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.385
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:15.251
Unit six: Reported Speech (basic). Today you will report what other people said.

4
00:00:15.551 --> 00:00:18.053
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.117
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:23.799
Said.

7
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:26.620
Said means the past of say.

8
00:00:27.217 --> 00:00:28.821
She said that she was tired.

9
00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:31.639
Your turn. Say: Said.

10
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:35.269
Said.

11
00:00:36.017 --> 00:00:36.786
Told.

12
00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:40.932
Told means the past of tell; used with a person.

13
00:00:41.517 --> 00:00:42.971
She told me a secret.

14
00:00:43.583 --> 00:00:45.934
Your turn. Say: Told.

15
00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:49.685
Told.

16
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:51.161
That.

17
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:54.788
That means can introduce a reported clause.

18
00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:56.814
He said that he was busy.

19
00:00:57.417 --> 00:01:00.150
Your turn. Say: That.

20
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.769
That.

21
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:05.436
Reported.

22
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.821
Reported means told to another person.

23
00:01:09.417 --> 00:01:11.289
Reported speech is indirect.

24
00:01:11.883 --> 00:01:14.443
Your turn. Say: Reported.

25
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:18.139
Reported.

26
00:01:18.883 --> 00:01:20.082
Direct speech.

27
00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:24.523
Direct speech means the exact words that someone says.

28
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.221
'I am tired' is direct speech.

29
00:01:27.817 --> 00:01:30.713
Your turn. Say: Direct speech.

30
00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:34.904
Direct speech.

31
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:36.663
Backshift.

32
00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:40.416
Backshift means moving the tense one step back.

33
00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:43.097
Backshift changes am into was.

34
00:01:43.683 --> 00:01:45.964
Your turn. Say: Backshift.

35
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:49.813
Backshift.

36
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:51.272
Quote.

37
00:01:52.283 --> 00:01:54.852
Quote means to repeat the exact words of someone.

38
00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:56.776
Please quote the author.

39
00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.036
Your turn. Say: Quote.

40
00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:03.576
Quote.

41
00:02:04.317 --> 00:02:05.538
Paraphrase.

42
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.525
Paraphrase means to express something in different words.

43
00:02:10.117 --> 00:02:11.629
Paraphrase the message.

44
00:02:12.217 --> 00:02:14.579
Your turn. Say: Paraphrase.

45
00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:18.643
Paraphrase.

46
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:23.537
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.383 --> 00:02:26.882
Visal, report what a friend recently told you.

48
00:02:27.983 --> 00:02:39.657
My friend told me that she was moving to Phnom Penh. In reported speech we usually move the tense one step back and change pronouns and time words.

49
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:42.332
How does the tense change?

50
00:02:43.417 --> 00:02:55.993
Present simple becomes past simple, present continuous becomes past continuous, present perfect becomes past perfect, will becomes would, and can becomes could.

51
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:58.177
Say or tell?

52
00:02:59.283 --> 00:03:12.970
Tell needs a person: She told me. Say does not: She said that. Time words change too: tomorrow becomes the next day. When the fact is still true, we can keep the present tense.

53
00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:16.040
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.883 --> 00:03:20.915
Grammar focus: Reported speech: said and told plus backshift.

55
00:03:21.215 --> 00:03:22.471
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.183 --> 00:03:25.520
She said that she was moving to Phnom Penh.

57
00:03:26.417 --> 00:03:28.347
He told me that he would call later.

58
00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:30.750
They said that they had finished.

59
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:38.915
Say that… or tell someone that… Move the tense one step back and change pronouns and time words. Tell needs a person; say does not.

60
00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:43.254
Be careful! Don't say: She said me that she was tired.

61
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.210
Say: She told me that she was tired.

62
00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:50.056
Use told with a person.

63
00:03:50.867 --> 00:03:53.623
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:55.957
Passing on a Message.

65
00:03:56.257 --> 00:03:58.941
My friend told me that she was moving to Phnom Penh.

66
00:03:59.933 --> 00:04:02.188
She said that she would call me every week.

67
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.931
The teacher told us that the test would be on Monday.

68
00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:11.406
Direct speech uses the exact words, but reported speech changes the tense.

69
00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.711
To paraphrase is to say the same message in different words.

70
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.871
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:21.717 --> 00:04:25.530
'I am tired,' she said. → She said she blank tired.

72
00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.984
A, is. B, was. C, will be.

73
00:04:32.533 --> 00:04:34.498
The answer is B: was.

74
00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:39.440
'I will call,' he said. → He said he blank call.

75
00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:42.639
A, will. B, would. C, can.

76
00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.083
The answer is B: would.

77
00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.099
She blank me that she was busy.

78
00:04:51.399 --> 00:04:54.878
A, said. B, told. C, say.

79
00:04:58.433 --> 00:05:00.131
The answer is B: told.

80
00:05:01.283 --> 00:05:02.818
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:05:03.118 --> 00:05:08.432
A, He said me he was ill.. B, He told me he was ill.. C, He told that he was ill..

82
00:05:11.967 --> 00:05:14.686
The answer is B: He told me he was ill..

83
00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:18.337
According to the reading, when would the test be?

84
00:05:18.637 --> 00:05:22.558
A, on Monday. B, on Friday. C, tomorrow.

85
00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.204
The answer is A: on Monday.

86
00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.482
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:33.317 --> 00:05:36.849
Report what a friend recently told you, using reported speech.

88
00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:47.057
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:47.357 --> 00:05:59.416
My friend told me that she was starting a new job next week. She said that she was excited but nervous. I use told with a person and move the tense one step back in reported speech.

90
00:05:59.716 --> 00:06:01.495
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:02.383 --> 00:06:08.089
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reported speech: said and told plus backshift.

92
00:06:08.389 --> 00:06:12.562
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

93
00:06:12.862 --> 00:06:15.306
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:15.606 --> 00:06:19.175
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

